{"text": "MLO2-2230\nJohn Joseph Almendarez\nTimeline for Identification\n\nJuly 2, 2002\nA body was found floating in Buffalo Bayou at 600 Lockwood. The Houston Police\nDepartment and the Investigations Division of the Harris County Medical Examiner's\nOffice (HCME) responded. The body was in a moderate state of decomposition and\nhad sustained water damage. The face was unrecognizable. The body was clad in a\ngreen T-shirt with a Houston Astros emblem and green cotton shorts with Nike\nemblem. No identification was found with the body. The body was assigned case\nnumber MLO2-2230 and transported to the HCME.\n\nJuly 3, 2002\nMLO2-2230 received an autopsy. Full body radiographs were imaged. The cause of\ndeath was pended for toxicology testing results. Due to the unidentified status,\nsamples of the head hair and a rib were retained for DNA testing. Attempts began to\nobtain legible fingerprints from the hands.\n\nuly 23-24, 2002\nFingerprints were submitted by fax to the FBI, TX Dept. of Public Safety, and the\nHarris County Sheriff's Office. The agencies requested that the fingerprints be\nmailed due to the poor definition caused by decomposition and water damage. The\nfingerprints were mailed on 7/24/2002.\n\nAugust 11, 2002\nBy this date, all the law enforcement agencies had all reported \u201cno hits\u201d on the\nfingerprints. Preparations began to ensure that all identifying information had been\nobtained prior to referring the decedent to the Harris County Bereavement\nDepartment for a county-assisted burial. The case information was supplied to the\nlocal media.\n\nSeptember 25, 2002\nThe pathologist classifies the cause and manner of death as: Asphyxia due to\nDrowning, Accident.\n\nApril 25, 2003\nThe consultant forensic odontologist examined and charted the dentition, took\ndental radiographs, and submitted a report to the HCME.\n\nAugust 12, 2003\nMLO2-2230 was entered into the NCIC (National Crime Information Center) database\nby TXDPS.\n\nanuary 5-7, 2004\nOn January 5, the facial skeleton was photographed in multiple views with a forensic\nruler to provide for potential facial approximation by an artist. On January 7, an\nadditional DNA sample (a finger bone) was removed from the decedent and",
